00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Çend sal in te karî asî (jenîn) orgê de berda ye?
 
How many years have you left the work of playing the
keyboard?

115
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Bi xwedê min neberda ye, ez min çê bû, yanî zerfek bû erê.
 
By God I haven't left it, I just had to, I mean it was a
circumstance, yes.

116
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Em hatin vira tine bû tişt. Û em çûn Tirkiyê, zatan em li
wira bûn.
 
We came here, there was nothing. And we went to Turkey,
basically we were there.

117
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Em li Îzmîrê bûn, yanî teşcîe... haflat ne muşecîe bûn wekî
Stanbolê ji te ra orgê bixwazî bînî de azfê bikî.
 
We were in Izmir, I mean encouragement... parties weren't
encouraging like in Istanbul for you to want to bring a
keyboard and play.

118
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Aman welleh, em di zarfê xwe da heyirî bûn, şixulê xwe da û
îşê xwe da. Heta fîl-fetrê taliyê, porîka me can, min ra
vebû.
 
Oh man by God, we were bewildered in our circumstances, in
our work and jobs. Until the last period, a little life
opened up for me.

119
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Yanî tu dihesî anî, nexasme fen jî, min jê terkî wî hes
nedikir, tiştekî me ke(r) bî.
 
I mean you feel it, especially art too, I didn't feel like
leaving it, it was a piece of us.

120
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Tu bîrî wî rojên din kî kekê Xalid?
 
Do you miss those days, brother Xalid?

121
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Bi xwedê, ez bi fexir... na bîrî dikim, ez bibêjim, bi fexir
yanî (ez serbilind im).
 
By God, with pride... no, I miss them, let me say, with
pride.

122
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Çima?
 
Why?

123
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Erê, lê ni... te xwestî û nexwestî jîleke we re(y) e, ekî
eyle şûnê me rûne.
 
Yes, because... whether you want it or not, there's a
generation after you, definitely they will take our place.

124
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

125
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Temam? Û jîl ser jîl ku îcbarî ecerer ke jî derkevî. Bilaks
em şan in, yanî noka meselan saheya fenî ya Efrînê me pêş...
pêş ketiye, destpêkê erê.
 
Okay? And generation after generation it's mandatory that
the wheel turns. On the contrary, we are proud, I mean now
for example the art scene of our Afrin has progressed... it
has advanced, compared to the beginning, yes.

126
00:11:46,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Yanî wekî em serdema destpêkê muqanaten em pir kişandin.
Yanî enî, org destpê bû tiştekî basît yanî tiştekî yanî vî,
dirase û vî ew, bas yavaş yavaş yavaş yavaş, hedekî xeber am
nav lêkir fena Efrîna hedîs, yanî we şanoya Efrîna hedîs a
ecer.
 
I mean when we compare it to our early era, we suffered a
lot. I mean, the keyboard was something simple at first, I
mean something, I mean this, studying and this and that, but
slowly, slowly, slowly, a bit of news we named the modern
art of Afrin, I mean the modern theater of Afrin.

127
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Belê kekê Xalid.
 
Yes brother Xalid.

128
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Ez bi fexir, ez însanî ku vî karî dibîm, bas min go min nav
orgçiyên me hebî, Efrînê... pê min jîlek derket. Ku niha
teqlîda min dikin.
 
With pride, I am a person who sees this work, but I said I
was among our keyboard players, of Afrin... a generation
came out after me. That now imitates me.

129
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Teqlîd mesela ê ... da dîtin Şêro û Menan kir, ez ne bîm
ere, ez jî min teqlîd waj dikir.
 
Imitating for example those... they saw what Şêro and Menan
did, I wasn't there, yes, I also imitated them a lot.

130
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Yanî her jîlek didê dinêrê mesela arşîvê orgçiyê, arşîvê
asîfê (azifê) orgê çi heye, pê digirin dinêrin, şûqê de derê
derbas dibe e.
 
I mean every generation comes, looks for example at the
archive of keyboard players, what is in the keyboard
player's archive, they take it, look at it, work on it and
move forward.

131
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

132
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Kekê Xalid, da gavê me ra bîrê bajarê xwe dikî çiqas tişt ji
me re tê der.
 
Brother Xalid, when you remember your city for us, so many
things come out.

133
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Te bîre te çiqas bîrî Efrînê kiribû gi strana 'De dîsa rabin
werin'?
 
Remember how much you missed Afrin when you sang the song
'Come, stand up again'?

134
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Hoho.
 
Oh wow.

135
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Peyv û sazê ne.
 
Words and music.

136
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Hemû jî ê te bîn.
 
They were all yours.

137
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Pir jî hene, em ê niha dest pê bikin.
 
There are many, we will start now.

138
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Kîjan, kîjan strana tefsîlatên wê te yozmîş kir.
 
Which one, which song did you write the details for.

139
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Destpêkê tiştek ji min re digot mehwîbeya min heye, yanî vî
meselê yozmîş kirinê. Xwendina min b'kurdî baş e. Yozmîş
kirina min baş e, rind e.
 
At first, something told me I have a talent, I mean for this
issue of writing. My reading in Kurdish is good. My writing
is good, it's nice.

140
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Yanî hîç kêmasî min nizanîbû, min yozmîştî dikir, dixwend.
 
I mean I knew no shortcomings at all, I was writing it,
reading it.

141
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Wekî dibînî, em welleh sidfê (bi tesadufî) tevî hev li wê
derê bûn... wî çaxî em li Îzmîrê azifê orgê, Xebat, silavên
min ji wî re hene, Hemedê Stêrk Xebat, silavên min ji wî re
hene, em pir dost bûn bi hev re.
 
As you can see, we were there together by chance... at that
time in Izmir the keyboard player, Xebat, my greetings to
him, Hemedê Stêrk Xebat, my greetings to him, we were very
good friends.

142
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Yanî şor şorê de derdixe, Xebat dest ere, azifê orgê ye,
nestire ya. Yanî nizam rojekê hinekî sitranan me got Xebat
welleh dengê te xweş e.
 
I mean words bring out words, Xebat got it, he's a keyboard
player, he doesn't sing. I mean I don't know, one day out of
nowhere I said, "Xebat, by God your voice is beautiful."

143
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

144
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Eynî honê, dengê te xweş e. Yanî enî, em xurt bûn em
derdiketin çolê, wextê me tenê bû (we were alone). Şixulê me
tu zanî ser telefonê ye, ferax (valatî) çêdibû, em
derdiketin, go "welleh nizanin kîjan got". Mi go "werim
stranek çêkin."
 
Just like that, your voice is beautiful. I mean, we were
young men going out into the nature, we had time alone. You
know our work was on the phone, when we had free time, we'd
go out. He said "By God I don't know who said it." I said
"Let's make a song."

145
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Hona hona. Hona hîn min dest bi tiştek nekiribû. Di vê
mubaderê de, stran dîsa dest pê bikin, tine bî welleh.
Welleh dest pê kirin...
 
Like this, like that. Like this I still hadn't started
anything. Through this initiative, to start songs again,
there was none by God. By God they started...

146
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Gû kî? Vî jî...
 
He said who? He also...

147
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Kî.
 
Who.

148
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Ma rabû, me dest pê kir ewil stranek me çêkir, ji wê saniyê
re, j' muntaleqê ku... ez xizmetek ji hevalê xwe ra bikim,
welleh.
 
So we got up, we started, we made the first song, from that
second, starting from the point that... I should do a
service for my friend, by God.

149
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Ewel stranek me dest pê kir, 'Eşqê Ta Dinya Kîdin e' (Your
love is another world).
 
The first song we started was 'Eşqa te dinyayeke din e'
(Your love is another world).

150
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
O wê selafê te yozmîş kir.
 
Oh, so you wrote the words for that one.

151
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Ewil stran min yozmîş kir, yanî êdî bi terîbeyê... tiştekî
yanî mi... na anî ez ekî têkivim mecalê tevda jî... 'Eşqa te
dinyayekî din e'.
 
The first song I wrote, I mean already by experience...
something that I... no, I didn't mean to enter this field
entirely... 'Your love is another world'.

152
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Û me çêkir, xwey da pa tab'en wî stranê derket. Û 'Azad Saz'
jî...
 
And we made it, and naturally that song came out. And 'Azad
Saz' too...

153
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Azad Saz jî wî... e...
 
Azad Saz too, he... er...

154
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Wî jî xizmet kir. Erê. Azad Saz jî telmîzê min bû.
 
He also served. Yes. Azad Saz was also my student.

155
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Haa.
 
I see.

156
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Fe yanî tîkele me çêbû, wî jî xwest xizmetekî bika...
wellahî min jî xizmetê xwe kir, derket, rind bû. Pir jê razî
bûn.
 
So I mean we mingled, he also wanted to do a service... by
God I also did my service, it came out, it was nice. They
were very satisfied with it.

157
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Sazê wî jî pir kêfxweş e, pir xweş e, û gotî wî jî pir xweş
derket.
 
His music is also very joyful, very beautiful, and his
singing also came out very beautiful.

158
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Û piştî wî de tu derbas bû, niha her dengbêjekê me Efrîn,
kekê, kê bixwezî, kî dengê xwe xweş be, kî daxwazî stranan
bêje, tê cem te, tu wî re yozmîş dikî.
 
And after that you moved forward, now every singer in our
Afrin, brother, whoever wants to, whoever has a good voice,
whoever wants to sing songs, comes to you, you write it for
them.

159
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:12,000
J'yek, stranê... Aslan Şêr. Gihîştê nîv milyon qet kiriye a.
 
Out of them, the song... Aslan Şêr. It reached half a
million, it broke it.

160
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Qet kiriye, erê qet kiriye. Va çawa hat, kesî ji te xwest,
yan te bi xwe yozmîş kir?
 
It broke it, yes it broke it. How did this come about, did
someone ask you for it, or did you write it yourself?

161
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Xelîl, kak... em niha li xerîbiyê... sidqen sidqen yanî em
bibînin efset (ebset) tefasîl... em ji hevdira da digirin.
 
Xelîl, brother... we are now in exile... honestly, honestly,
I mean we see the simplest details... we grab onto them from
each other.

162
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Li vê derê, yanî însanê ku wekî derket, gundek taswîr dikir,
ku leqtekî (dîmenek) çûçik me li gundekî didî (didît), yanî
dilê me wê derê dadigirî (dadigirt).
 
Here, I mean a person who went out as if he was picturing a
village, when we saw a small glimpse of a village, I mean
our hearts would attach to that place.

163
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Ev yeko (noqteyek). Piştî tehrîr çêdibe, milet vedigere mala
xwe... wextî milet fitilî û milet nefitilî, hino jî, ji xwe
re ser wan tiştekî, îh jî dilê mi derket lo... hîsasek
derket... kê bi wan ra tewasil dibe?
 
This is one point. After the liberation happens, the people
return to their homes... when the people returned and the
people didn't return, somehow, something came out of my
heart about it man... a feeling came out... who communicates
with them?

164
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Ew kuş (dîmen) dildar e, me bi xwe ra didan kişandin...
xwarzê min û apê min... Akoş. Temam tu çûyî cem ehbabên min
jî, pir bêriya gundê xwe dikiya (dikir)... fe hav (lewra
ev), xelef stûqalê min (zêde hesreta min) xiste (zêde kir),
teqelê (hesreta) min zêde bî (bû). Em zûyî gihîştine hev.
 
That scene is lovely, we were pulling it towards
ourselves... my nephew and my uncle... Akoş. Fine, you went
to my loved ones too, you missed your village a lot... so
this, added to my longing, my longing increased. We soon
reached each other.

165
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Min go "xwarzê", min go "xwarzê. Lo! Ka em tiştekî wênikî
bikin?"
 
I said "Nephew", I said "Nephew. Man! Let's do something
like this?"

166
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Min go "welleh miletî d'fetile û ka asanî kiç (kî dikare)
biçe?"
 
I said "By God the people are returning and who can easily
go?"

167
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Go welleh rind e. Û wî jî tecîh (teşcî) kirim.
 
He said "By God it's nice." And he also encouraged me.

168
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:13,000
E, teşcî kirim. Me rabî, berî wê jî, stranê tebê xêra te bi,
'Bûkam' ya Eslan Şêr.
 
Yes, he encouraged me. We got up, and before that too, the
song may it be to your goodness, 'My bride' by Eslan Şêr.

169
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Ew hazir bî.
 
That one was ready.

170
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Hazir bî. Hîn da neketibû... Hazir bî, em tenê 'Aslan
sekinîbû' heta zerfek munasib... da xwîne, silavên mi ji
Aslan ra hene, pir j'hez dikim Aslan. Dengê wî jî hez dikim
ji bêjda (ji stranbêjiya wî)... yanî hîn am hêvî li hev da
qewimîn na jî.
 
It was ready. It hadn't come out yet... It was ready, we
were just 'waiting for Aslan' until a suitable
circumstance... so he could sing, my greetings to Aslan, I
like Aslan a lot. I also like his voice and his singing... I
mean still, we were hoping for it to happen together.

171
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,000
De dîsa rabin Efrîniyên xwe şên bikin, min hazir kir, min
şand
 
'Come stand up again, make your Afrin flourish', I prepared
it, I sent it.

172
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Bo mamosta Akoş dildar.
 
To teacher Akoş Dildar.

173
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Min şand, derbê (yekser)... hal meselan hona. Dereksûn de
(Di eynî demê de) got "welleh," got "Xalid," delalo got
"welleh mirûzê mi nemaye," yanî ser stranên wilo (hona).
 
I sent it, immediately... for example like this. At the same
time he said "By God," he said "Xalid," dear he said "By God
I have no mood left," I mean for songs like this.

174
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

175
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,000
G'mirûzê min ser stranan nemaye.
 
He said 'I have no mood left for songs'.

176
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Pêşî, min ev jî nîşan da, yanî nîda aka (bangewaziyek) jî
min xwend, min go... yanî gişt rabin... ji kefa fîetên (ji
hemû fîetên) muctemah, em rabin werin.
 
First, I also showed this, I mean I read a call out too, I
said... I mean everyone stand up... from all parts of
society, let's stand up and come.

177
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
De dîsa werin e.
 
'Stand up and come again'.

178
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:59,000
Rab'n am Efrîna xwe şên b'k'n. Çi hebû, çi tinabî, çi hebû,
çi tinabî.
 
Stand up, let's make our Afrin flourish. Whatever there was,
whatever there wasn't, whatever there was, whatever there
wasn't.

179
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Em dîsa geşbîn b'k'n.
 
Let's make it optimistic again.

180
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Am dîsa geşbîn bikin.
 
Let's make it optimistic again.

181
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Yanî wê gotinê bizzat 'Çi hebû çi tinebû', yanî ê... ê bûbû
û ê nebû nebû, çi bû çi nebû, heyat ge 'stimrar me be (jiyan
wê berdewam be), heyat ke bimeşe, fe eger ek zora... (fe
eger em li pey bin) em giş ji bîra bikin, em heyata xwe dest
pê bikin.
 
I mean this exact phrase 'Whatever there was, whatever there
wasn't', I mean uh... what happened happened, and what
didn't didn't, whatever happened whatever didn't happen,
life will continue, life will go on, so if we push... let's
forget it all, let's start our life.

182
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Fa (lewra) elhemdulilah... çaxê wilo got, û aslen j'
têkeliya min li ser vî stranê pir me daxwaz kir...
 
So thank God... when he said that, and basically my
connection to this song, we requested it a lot...

183
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Stran... ba'dê te yozmîş kir, min gotina te qet kir ku
mamoste... Stran te berî ku yozmîş kir ji mamosteyê me Akoş
re bû?
 
The song... after you wrote it, I cut your word that
teacher... Was the song for our teacher Akoş before you
wrote it?

184
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

185
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Gendî jîne b'bir... te da Aslan. (Kengî jê xeber nebû te da
Aslan.)
 
When there was no word from him, you gave it to Aslan.

186
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Got "Ez yanî vî şexefê (şewqê) mi nemaye, we ew me nemaye."
Na mebdeyî ne eciz bûn dibî (nedibû), nê nê mebdeyî got ne
mesela aciz bûn e, hin weh hadîs derneket... "Na m's'la
muareza yî sar tiştekî j'." Wellehî.
 
He said "I mean I don't have this passion anymore, I don't
have that anymore." Not that he was upset on principle, no
no on principle he said it's not a matter of being upset,
these words didn't come out yet... "Not a matter of opposing
something either." By God.

187
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Heqê xwo bir s'tran e.
 
He did the song justice.

188
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Erê paşê me go, "Aslan... hal mesele." Go "wellehel azîm
xalid!" Go, "as ji te dî dî'r e, hsasiyê min vê tiştê
d'gerê!"
 
Yes then I said, "Aslan... this is the situation." He said
"By Almighty God, Xalid!" He said, "I have been seeing this
for a long time, my feelings are looking for this thing!"

189
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

190
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Subhanellah. Û hema şev (şevê), roja keda (roja din) cem
Xelîl meselan ji lezand, tê Xelîl Xilo... birayekî me yê
ezîz e ew jî.
 
Glory be to God. And that very night, the next day with
Xelîl for example he hurried up, Xelîl Xilo comes... he is a
dear brother of ours too.

191
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Meselan (Mesela) lezand. Teswîr (wênegirtin) xilas pê bî
(bû), hîn ew (stûdiyo) xilas nebibî ev stran.
 
For example, he hurried. The filming was finished, even
before the studio work of the song was finished.

192
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Heta nih (niha) welleh me rabî ser xwa... orê ser avda anî,
daxistin e... maşellah, yanî fetre(yek) kinik de, rabî. Û
heta noka (niha) jî radibe. Fe pir pir xweş e.
 
Up until now by God we stood up... we brought it out to the
open, downloaded it... Mashallah, I mean in a short period,
it rose. And up until now it is still rising. So it's very
very beautiful.

193
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Û bi wê xweşiya stranê, piştî milet vegeriya jî nuha gilî
nîn e, lewre gotinên wê stranê jî pir xweş e.
 
And with the beauty of that song, after the people returned
too there are no complaints now, because the words of that
song are also very beautiful.

194
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Jî piştî wê jî te pir stran çêkirine, ji kekê Enwer re te
çêkiriye, ji De Biharê re...
 
Also, after that you made a lot of songs, you made them for
brother Enwer, for 'Come Spring'...

195
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Erê... ew jî... Kakê Enwer qesed heyatê min e bibînim.
Teqrîben yanî ez eyaşa tefûliya xwe... j'nêv beriya kolkê
min, bavê, bapîrê min... û bavê... dêkê min (dayika min).
Tiştek û ez bibêjim... kulbeyek ame (a me), ewa noka mala
Mamostê ye (amo zad e).
 
Yes... that too... Brother Enwer, it's a story of my life if
I may say. Mostly I mean, I live my childhood... from within
the plains of my hut, my father's, my grandfather's... and
the father... of my mother. A thing and let me say... a hut
of ours, that is now the house of my cousin.

196
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Erê... wextî em diçûn zeytûnê, wextê ku anî, ew dar
